    "introduction": "Rolls-Royce designs and supports engines and power systems for civil aviation, defence and industrial applications. Its civil aerospace business supplies engines for large passenger aircraft and business jets, then maintains them over operating lives that can extend for decades. Defence activities include military aircraft propulsion and naval power systems, while mtu-branded products serve applications such as backup power and marine propulsion. Revenue combines equipment sales with servicing, spare parts and long-term support agreements. Aircraft utilisation therefore matters alongside new engine deliveries. Engineering capability, product reliability and maintenance efficiency are central to the business, which requires sustained investment in technology and manufacturing.",
